Using the LVGL module on top of the :external+zephyr:ref:`Display driver API
<display_api>` with chosen display. That is:

| :hwftlbl-scr:`LCD` : :dts:`chosen { zephyr,display = &lcd_panel; };`
| :hwftlbl-scr:`ILI9341` : :dts:`lcd_panel: &ili9341_240x320 {};`

.. rubric:: Devicetree compatible

- :dtcompatible:`zephyr,mipi-dbi-spi`

.. tabs::

   .. zephyr-keep-sorted-start re(^\s{9}\.\. group-tab:: \w)

   .. group-tab:: Arduino Nano R3

      If the shield is connected to a board which has Arduino Nano
      connector, set :console:`-DSHIELD=waveshare_2_4_lcd` when you
      invoke :program:`west build`. For example:

      .. zephyr-app-commands::
         :app: zephyr/samples/subsys/display/lvgl
         :build-dir: waveshare_2_4_lcd-lvgl_basic
         :board: cytron_maker_nano_rp2040
         :shield: "waveshare_2_4_lcd"
         :snippets: "usb-console"
         :gen-args: \
            -DCONFIG_REGULATOR_SHELL=y
         :west-args: -p
         :flash-args: -r uf2
         :goals: flash
         :host-os: unix

   .. group-tab:: Grove System

      If the shield is connected to a board which has
      `Grove System`_ compatiple connectors, set
      :console:`-DSHIELD=waveshare_2_4_lcd` when you invoke
      :program:`west build` and use one of supported boards with
      special Devicetree setup for free wiring. For example:

      .. zephyr-app-commands::
         :app: zephyr/samples/subsys/display/lvgl
         :build-dir: waveshare_2_4_lcd-lvgl_basic
         :board: cytron_maker_pi_rp2040
         :shield: "waveshare_2_4_lcd"
         :snippets: "usb-console"
         :gen-args: \
            -DCONFIG_REGULATOR_SHELL=y
         :west-args: -p
         :flash-args: -r uf2
         :goals: flash
         :host-os: unix

   .. zephyr-keep-sorted-stop

.. rubric:: Simple test execution on target

(text in bold is a command input)

.. container:: highlight highlight-console notranslate no-copybutton

   .. parsed-literal::

      \*\*\* Booting Zephyr OS build |zephyr_version_em|\ *…*\*\*\*
      :bgn:`uart:~$` **█**

.. rubric:: Basics

Device listing:

   .. container:: highlight highlight-console notranslate

      .. parsed-literal::

         :bgn:`uart:~$` **device list**
         devices:
         … … …
         - lcd-backlight-en (READY)
           DT node labels: lcd_backlight_en
         - mipi-dbi (READY)
           DT node labels: mipi_dbi
         - ili9341-320x240\ @\ 0 (READY)
           DT node labels: ili9341_320x240 lcd_panel
         - gpio-keys (READY)
           DT node labels: gpio_keys
         - lvgl-keypad (READY)
           DT node labels: lvgl_keypad

.. rubric:: LCD backlight

Operate with the LCD backlight switch as voltage regulator:

   .. container:: highlight highlight-console notranslate

      .. parsed-literal::

         :bgn:`uart:~$` **regulator vlist lcd-backlight-en**
         3.300000 V
         0 uV

   .. container:: highlight highlight-console notranslate

      .. parsed-literal::

         :bgn:`uart:~$` **regulator vget lcd-backlight-en**
         3.300000 V

   The off/on sequence:

   .. container:: highlight highlight-console notranslate

      .. parsed-literal::

         :bgn:`uart:~$` **regulator vset lcd-backlight-en 0V**

   .. container:: highlight highlight-console notranslate

      .. parsed-literal::

         :bgn:`uart:~$` **regulator vset lcd-backlight-en 3300mV**

